the saints reboot is finally here and  even though the game is pretty  self-explanatory there are a couple  things that took me a while to figure  out and i want you to skip that step so  here are seven things i wish i knew when  i first started playing saints row  one thing you should know about me is  that i love to spend about an hour with  the game's character creator it's the  perfectionist in me i'm also guilty of  restarting games because i don't like  the way my character looks but whether  you're like me or not i'm here to tell  you that you shouldn't spend more than 5  minutes in the saints row character  creator for starters the boss factory  demo aka the creation tools were out  months before the game so you should  have already spent hours recreating  yourself my other reason for saying this  is because you'll have all of the same  options at your disposal at any point in  the game the only exceptions are when  you're driving and flying otherwise you  can be in the middle of a gunfight  editing the size of your hips as you get  shot it's also worth noting that your  character is going to be in a uniform  with a helmet on for the entire first  mission so it doesn't really matter what  they look like pick a voice that you  think you'll want to hear for those  initial dialogue sequences and just drop  right into the action guns blazing  see i'm flanking left as ordered  when i started saints row on console i  was immediately dissatisfied with the  sensitivity of my aim and was equally  disappointed when i could not find an  option to lower it unbeknownst to me the  option was in fact available just not  where i expected it to be initially i  was looking in the controls menu for  ways to change my aim but that only  provided a stick dead zone option so for  a while my workaround was to go into  options gameplay and then challenge  options this menu not only lets you dial  in the difficulty of things like vehicle  combat and enemy durability but you can  also customize how much help the game's  aim assist will be the default lock on  type is short lock but i found that  switching to full lock was exactly what  i needed to start enjoying combat more  some players might even benefit from  leaving it on short lock but increasing  the lock-on attraction to wide however  if you'd rather change the sensitivity  like i wanted to at first that option is  hidden in the camera settings there's  duplicate menu options all over the  place but for some reason sensitivity  only shows up in this one spot  a large chunk of building your criminal  empire in saints row comes from starting  businesses and using them as fronts for  illegal activity these businesses called  criminal ventures in game can often be  the key to unlocking new story missions  and side activities like insurance fraud  so i'd advise buying as many as you can  early on during my playthrough i was  locked out of a mission with eli and  could not figure out why that was the  case until i finally returned to the  criminal ventures table and realized  what i had to build was there as an  option and even though these businesses  can be pricey don't think of it as a  waste of your hard-earned cash because  they all make you hourly income once  they're up and running it won't be long  before you've earned back what you spent  and then some especially if you  eliminate the threats around each one  because that increases the hourly income  that can be earned just don't forget to  transfer your funds from the cash app on  your in-game phone  fast travel in saints row isn't hard but  it's not completely obvious so other  than your apartment and eventually the  saints hq you can teleport to four  additional points in santo aliso these  points are marked by a purple icon with  a subway car as the image to activate  these points you'll need to take a  picture of the landmark there seems  simple enough right well during my  playthrough i ran into a small issue  where the guidelines weren't showing up  for me this was mostly a problem at the  panther rock fast travel point to fix  this i just walked around the path a  little bit away from the exact point  that the icon was showing on the map and  then it finally triggered the photo to  work but hopefully this was just a small  pre-launch issue that was fixed with the  game's day one patch  stealing cars is cool and all but owning  one is even cooler why because you can  customize the car and make it your own  no more nabbing brenda's car at a red  light and having to be seen driving  around with her lame rims this is why  garages are your best friend at the  start of the game there's one right next  to your apartment building you can store  cars here and access them anytime you  return after that you'll find an auto  body shop of sorts on the side of the  church that can be used for the same  purpose but at this point you'll also  have gym rob's garage as well  unfortunately both of these are on the  same side of the city so you have to  drive whatever you want to keep all the  way around to either location but these  garages can do more than storing cars  and making them look nice they are also  where you can upgrade cars alongside the  upgrades are signature abilities special  for lack of a better term abilities that  can be unlocked by completing challenges  associated with that vehicle i overlook  these way longer than i care to admit so  i suggest you take advantage of them as  soon as you can because some of them are  capable of adding a small layer of  variety to the traversal and vehicle  combat  it took me way too long to upgrade my  weapons during my playthrough this  wasn't a huge inconvenience as it didn't  cause me to constantly fail missions but  the fact is stronger weapons make combat  a little bit more fun so don't just look  at friendly fire gun shops around town  as places to purchase new weapons look  at them as a place to customize and  upgrade your arsenal as well similar to  vehicles weapons also have signature  abilities and friendly fire is one spot  you can enable those abilities for each  weapon as you unlock them and in order  to do that you have to complete the  challenges associated with that weapon  the stagecoach shotgun for example has a  buffalo shot ability that can be  unlocked by killing five martial  gunslingers with the stagecoach the  faster you complete the challenge the  faster you have access to just one more  way of making you an unstoppable force  two useful parts of saints row are  skills and perks that can be equipped  once unlocked after completing special  challenges something that i wish i did  immediately upon starting the game is  completing these challenges on purpose  what i mean by this is a handful of  these challenges are finished over time  by just simply playing the game for  example making a purchase at a shop or  traveling a certain distance by car or  by foot i reached each of these goals  passively but if i looked over the  objectives and finished them on purpose  instead i could have leveled up my  character and unlocked the skills and  perks associated with each level of  challenge much quicker so those are the  things i wish i knew when i first  started playing saints rock they aren't  completely game changing but each one is  enough to save you a decent amount of  time early on so what are some of the  things that took you way too long to  figure out that would help someone else  let us know in the comments and like  this video if you found it helpful at  all you can find me on twitter at  devonta chisholm thanks for watching  oh  foreign
 

